## Version and failure behavior

Every root payload requires explicit `schema_version: 1.0.0` and `synthetic: true`. Unknown fields, incompatible schema versions, booleans in numeric fields, string-to-number coercion and nonfinite values are rejected by strict Pydantic validation. VersionRef includes an ID, exact version string and SHA-256 reference; semantic changes require a new version and invalidate dependent evidence, preserving historical artifacts. Runtime accepted-reference catalogs must be supplied to `validate_fit_request` before scheduling costly work; no default backend/configuration substitution occurs. Artifact hash calculation/import/shape enforcement is still G0-LIB/G2; a syntactically valid hash is not proof an artifact exists or matches.

Numeric estimates are separate discriminated states from undefined, failed, abstained, pending, inconclusive and prior-only. Unavailable states have a reason and cannot carry an invented estimate. Fit metadata preserves explicit backend/sampler/package versions, float64 precision, diagnostics references and accepted/failed/abstained/pending status. PyMC/native NUTS is the only current fit-request backend/sampler. No PyMC package was installed or fitted in this task. G2/G5 still own runtime enforcement, real metadata round-trip and observed rejection before actual costly worker invocation under LIB-03.

## Temporal and lineage decisions for review

The versioned temporal manifest names equation parents, units, visibility and roles before/after each estimand's assignment. Same-day parents must precede their children; lagged parents cannot refer to future days. Clinical L is a current covariate and later mediator; prognostic latent random effects never replace measured confounders or directly drive assignment. Exogenous innovations are separate process-keyed draws, not shared noise. Initial distributions, irregular-visit law, all unprovided coefficients, observation/event processes and scenario overrides must be completed/reviewed by G0-DGP before generation.

The following reversible synthetic engineering conventions are explicit proposals:

1. Instants are timezone-aware and ordered in UTC. The integer synthetic day grid represents fixed 24-hour days; local calendar dates, timezone labels and overnight episode endpoints remain separate display/adapter metadata. A source adapter must normalize event/recorded/available times so `event <= recorded <= available`; original source/device times remain in the source payload and hash. This is conservative server-ingestion availability, not a vendor schema guarantee. Supported timezone-database handling and real adapter mapping remain G1 qualification.
2. Morning measurements of the previous night precede same-day decisions. A learner history includes only events at/before cutoff with server-recorded and available timestamps **strictly before** cutoff. Equal timestamps are conservatively excluded from model input. Phase then stable record ID makes replay deterministic. Known current holds and consent withdrawals are administrative guards with precedence before a draw, including an update exactly at draw time; model history filtering cannot override a current hold.
3. TIME-01 v2 full order: prior-night morning measurement event and separate wearable availability â†’ current clinical L and independent observed pain â†’ strictly available pre-report history â†’ report-observation/recording decision â†’ report upload availability â†’ later available decision history â†’ recorded interruptions/current consent/holds â†’ eligibility â†’ scheduled visit assignment â†’ N-of-1 assignment where applicable â†’ support availability/final propensity/assignment â†’ delivery/taken/rescue â†’ skills/carryover/rebound â†’ overnight severity â†’ next-morning quality/function/recall. The historical v1 manifest is preserved, with its earlier aggregate availability-before-L order; new consumers require explicit accepted v2 version/hash selection. The structural manifest permits evaluator-only latent causes for generation; learner decisions receive only allowed observed history. Fatigue uses the previous morning, never a future reward. Admission/death suspend subsequent assignments through current state guards; actual transactional event ingestion is G1/G5 work.

The v2 reporting boundary is proposed in `temporal-v2.json`, `ReportingRules` and `ReportingDecision`; wire schema remains1.0.0. A provisional07:00 outcome-event /08:00 pain-observation /08:01 report-decision clock separates clinical observation from report receipt. The pain ID must resolve to an active independent clinical `Observation` in the validated `LearnerHistory`, observed after the outcome event and strictly available before the report decision. A `DailyReport` or hidden truth payload cannot substitute. `mar_predictors()` returns only latest earlier observed report quality, its missing-history indicator (baseline7 when absent), and observed pain; it never returns current quality, wearable proxies or latent L. This is a pure observed-MAR input contract, not an implementation of missingness probabilities/calibration. MNAR structural generation remains evaluator-only in G0-DGP.

Report recording equals its observation-decision time; available time equals recording plus an explicitly declared0/1/3-day delay. The current report is absent from pre-report history. Earlier reports arriving exactly at the decision time are excluded, regardless of replay ties; later snapshots can include them. Previous quality is selected by event time then available/recorded time and stable record ID, independent of input-list order. Wearable availability never waits for report/pain and is not a MAR predictor. Proposed clocks/delays are explicit synthetic engineering choices; v2 requires independent exact-head/base acceptance before DGP consumption. Existing entity shapes, strict cutoffs, correction lineage, recall, consent/hold and no-postdeath rules are preserved.
4. ISI carries seven integer items 0â€“4, instrument version and explicit 14- or 30-day recall instants. Total is calculated, never independently supplied. Synthetic recall uses complete fixed-day intervals; `validate_isi_endpoint` requires matching version/recall and a wholly postassignment window. The first scheduled assessment satisfying that rule is eligible; no early administration mixing preassignment nights becomes an assignment endpoint. Day-42 visit/interruption horizon remains required; exact calendar/visit bindings belong to G0-DGP. Different versions/recall intervals cannot be trended together.
5. Corrections retain event time, patient, kind and lineage, advance revision and reference exactly one predecessor. Availability controls supersession: later corrections do not alter earlier as-known views. Duplicates reference an earlier original payload/hash and are omitted from the learner view. Retractions remove the lineage only when available. Immutable persisted snapshots, source hash verification and OS/process denial of evaluator storage remain G1/G5 obligations; these pure validators do not provide storage isolation.

## Estimands and outcomes

The registry proposes semantic version 1.0.0 for EST-VISIT, EST-N1, EST-ESC-STAGE, EST-ESC-STRATEGY, EST-MRT, EST-POLICY and EST-INT. Concrete runs must bind accepted population/eligibility, data/prior/model/DGP/scenario/protocol hashes, time zero/cutoff, intervention/comparator, units/direction, endpoint and common continuation/support mappings. N-of-1 uses reversible MED_A versus MED_B assignment; behavioral escalation preserves skills and distinguishes stage from strategy using distinct versioned embedded-regime references; MRT causal excursion differs from fixed contextual/cohort policy value, whose target kind and two policy versions are explicit. Protocol block/stage/cohort horizons refer to explicit versioned protocols; this package introduces no numeric block lengths or escalation rules. Fixture hashes/protocols are plainly artificial and cannot enter an accepted reference catalog.

Death uses separate survival plus conditional symptoms; admission uses admission/alive-outpatient probabilities plus conditional symptoms; regimen/steroid changes, rescue, discontinuation and overrides use treatment policy. No adherer restriction silently replaces the assignment estimand. EST-INT returns separate day-42 survival, admission, alive-outpatient and intervention-specific conditional ISI with event times. Conditional Monte Carlo counts retain total and conditioning counts; zero conditioning probability/count yields undefined ISI. There is no common-survivor interpretation, scalar utility or automatic overall winner. No ISI or daily symptom outcome is accepted after a nonretracted death event.

Ordinary approval selects one eligible option. Randomization approval authorizes a set without preselecting a winner; assignments retain the drawn option/probability/seed, blinding and any separately recorded eligible override. Per-component consent/oversight is checked against the latest available current record. These pure checks are contract fixtures; authentication, ownership, atomic transactions, idempotency, race handling and persisted approval are future G5 acceptance.

Threshold contracts require a name/version/unit, provisional synthetic engineering provenance and deferred clinical review. No numerical benefit threshold was chosen. Real literature evidence stays rationale-only, separate from synthetic quantitative trials. External studies admit IPD or a summary likelihood, excluding duplicate use of both. All sources, seed namespaces, allowed information, comparator assumptions and failure policy are typed; truth estimates/SEs in evaluator fixtures are analytic examples, not empirical results.

